{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/567525-mr-robot","id":567525,"title":"Mr. Robot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T00:37:45-07:00","id":567525,"title":"Mr. Robot","content":"So the pilot episode of this new series had its official premiere and immediately a lot of WoD triggers in my brain got tripped. There's nothing overtly supernatural in it, E(vil) Corp isn't quite the Seers of the Throne or the God-Machine, but still it got me thinking. Mild spoilers may follow.<br /> <br /> If I were to adapt it to DtD, I would say that Eliot is/was a Guardian angel (though admittedly not in the traditional sense: he works for an e-security company) but started pushing the limits of his mission beyond the original parameters, hacking information in order to protect individuals he knows personally or just trying to &quot;improve&quot; the God-Machine's status quo in general. His cover wasn't created to be especially deep and was thus tailor-made to minimize and avoid personal attachments, but the developing sense of the world's unfairness has left him teetering on the edge of Falling for some time now.<br /> <br /> Then the Saboteur called Mr. Robot decides to try giving him a little nudge...<br /> <br /> Eliot could also work just as well as a vanilla mortal stumbling onto the barest glimpse of a major conspiracy in the World of Darkness. (I would still suggest Mr. Robot as either some stripe of Unchained looking for a human ally or a mage of the Free Council trying to possibly push him into Awakening in that case.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,",